On Jan 17, 2007, at 6:02 PM, Pierre Abbat wrote:

> {noltruti'u} is one word. {noltru ti'u le cupra}... (is something  
> very other)

I'm concerned about a basic thing here: was audio/visual isomorphism  
dropped along the line? (I don't want to reopen any old wars if so.)

It seems to me that a person reading aloud would pronounce  
{noltruti'u} and {noltru ti'u} exactly the same, or too closely for a  
human or computer to distinguish them. But you (also Ted) say there's  
a semantic difference.

Should {nobli turni tixnu} ==  "Princess" be noltruNti'u or such, to  
keep CC glue joints?

DC



  


